        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · Americas</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Maya civilisation</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán Peninsula</a> and the lands to its south: south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiapas">Chiapas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabasco">Tabasco</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a>, Yucatán and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintana-roo">Quintana Roo</a>), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, Belize and the western parts of Honduras and El Salvador</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 2000 BCE–1697 CE: the Preclassic period until c. 250 CE, the Classic c. 250–900, and the Postclassic until the Spanish conquest, completed with the fall of Nojpetén in 1697</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Hieroglyphic writing, the Long Count calendar and astronomy; temple-pyramids and palaces at Tikal, Palenque, Copán and Chichén Itzá; rival dynasties of holy kings; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/classic-maya-collapse">Classic Maya collapse</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">The ruined cities and their inscriptions, most of which can now be read; four surviving pre-conquest books; Spanish accounts such as that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-landa">Diego de Landa</a>; colonial writings in Maya languages, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/popol-vuh">Popol Vuh</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/books-of-chilam-balam">Books of Chilam Balam</a>; the living Maya peoples</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="empire-meta">10 min read · Last reviewed October 2026</p>
